\title{thangldKANr: Kolmogorov-Arnold Networks with Interchangeable Edge Bases
Using 'torch'}
\description{
One network engine, many edge types. \code{\link[=thangld_kan]{thangld_kan()}} builds a network whose
edge functions use one of the built-in bases (Chebyshev, Gaussian RBF as
in FastKAN, Legendre, Mexican-hat wavelet, safe Pade rational, hybrid
SiLU + Chebyshev + RBF, Jacobi, squared-ReLU bumps), possibly a different
basis in each layer. Other packages add bases with
\code{\link[=register_kan_basis]{register_kan_basis()}}. The same layers are used by
\code{\link[=thangld_graph_kan]{thangld_graph_kan()}} (node regression on a graph) and
\code{\link[=thangld_temporal_kan]{thangld_temporal_kan()}} (one-step forecasts from lag windows).
}
